  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-forensic art direction, crisp headline hierarchy, restrained cyan/red semantics, and consistent card styling across viewports. However, tablet and mobile lose the desktop’s connected evidence-flow composition: cards become a long, visually sparse stack, with awkward dead space around the connectors. Desktop also leaves excessive unused lower space. The global header is cramped and visibly clipped on tablet/mobile, while tiny, low-contrast monospaced labels weaken readability and polish. Mobile’s narrative becomes especially tall and mechanically stacked rather than deliberately composed.",
    "fix": "Recompose the tablet/mobile evidence trail as a tighter, clearly connected sequence; reduce vertical dead space; strengthen small-label contrast and size; and redesign the responsive header with an intentional compact navigation pattern instead of clipped horizontal content.",
